sshteam-lib CHANGES
===================

This file records notable changes for sshteam-lib by release.

Version 0.0.1
-------------
Initial public baseline release.

Core features:
- DPoP proof generation and signing via DpopSigner.
  - Generates EC P-256 key pairs.
  - Creates RFC 9449-style DPoP proofs for token and resource endpoints.
  - Supports serializing/restoring private JWK material.
- HTTP client for SSH Teams server API via SshteamHttpClient.
  - OAuth2 device authorization start and token polling.
  - Token refresh flow.
  - SSH certificate signing request endpoint.
  - Device revocation endpoint.
  - Server URL helpers for sign/token/revoke routes.
- Multi-server credential abstraction via DeviceStore.
  - Per-server credential persistence contract.
  - Default server selection.
  - Access token refresh convenience logic.
  - DPoP key storage/loading contract.
- DeviceCredentials value object for access token, refresh token, expiry, and key id.
- ServerUrlNormalizer utility for consistent base URL handling.

Compatibility notes:
- Java 11+ baseline.
- No high-level workflow facade in this release; consumers orchestrate raw flow steps themselves.


Version 0.0.2-SNAPSHOT
----------------------
This version adds a higher-level client API and extensible encrypted persistence primitives.

Added:
- New high-level facade: SshteamClient.
  - startRegistration(...)
  - register(...)
  - pollRegistration(...)
  - getCurrentAccessToken()
  - requestCertificate(...)
  - revokeDevice(...)
  - listRegistrations(), listRegistrationsAsMaps()
- Registration scope convenience defaults.
  - DEFAULT_REGISTRATION_SCOPE = signing.
  - Overloads that no longer require explicitly passing scope.
- Ephemeral SSH certificate helper.
  - generateEphemeralCertificate(host, port, username, keyType)
  - Probes remote SSH host key fingerprint.
  - Generates ephemeral keypair.
  - Requests SSH Teams certificate.
  - Returns combined SshKeyPair (private key + signed certificate key).
- New reusable file-backed store base:
  - AbstractFileDeviceStore
  - Standardized per-server path layout.
  - Encrypted token save/load pattern with enc:: prefix handling.
  - Default server metadata persistence.
  - Best-effort restrictive file permissions.
- New encryption abstraction and implementation:
  - DeviceStoreEncryption (pluggable strategy interface)
  - AesGcmDeviceStoreEncryption (Java 11 compatible AES/GCM)
  - Per-server key derivation from caller-supplied secret material.
- New integration-style tests for high-level flows:
  - SshteamClientIntegrationTest
  - InMemoryDeviceStore test double

Changed:
- pom version updated from 0.0.1 to 0.0.2-SNAPSHOT.
- Added Maven dependency:
  - com.sshtools:maverick-synergy-client:${maverick.version}
- Added property:
  - maverick.version=3.2.0-SNAPSHOT
- DeviceStore docs now point file-backed implementations to AbstractFileDeviceStore + DeviceStoreEncryption.

Behavioral notes:
- Existing DeviceStore method signatures remain unchanged (additive evolution).
- generateEphemeralCertificate requires network reachability to the target SSH host/port.
- Encryption is now explicitly consumer-configurable through DeviceStoreEncryption.

Potential upgrade impact:
- Projects requiring deterministic/release-only dependencies should review snapshot usage of maverick-synergy-client.
- Consumers may migrate from ad hoc orchestration to SshteamClient for simpler registration and cert workflows.
